WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.967
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:02.969
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:03.969
We hope you're all doing well

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:04.970
and let's get to the news.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.573
Facebook went offline yesterday

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:08.774
for over six hours.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.977
Wow, they finally
found something

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.946
they couldn't fix
with horse paste.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.214
[ Laughter ]
Facebook apologized yesterday

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.283
after all three
of its social media platforms

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.353
went offline for six hours
and said it was due

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.556
to a "faulty
configuration change,"

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.191
adding, "after a quick reboot,

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.759
he started working again."

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.761
[ Laughter ]
President Biden said yesterday

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:31.097
that he couldn't guarantee
that the federal government

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:34.534
will not default on debt
payments due later this month.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.736
So, in addition to everything
else going on, we've now entered

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:40.940
the "Uncut Gems" phase
of his presidency.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.409
[ Laughter ]
Right now, he's on the phone
to de Blasio, saying --

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:46.012
[ As Biden ]
Put all of Montana on red!

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.747
[ Laughter ]
During a Zoom session yesterday

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.248
with the
House Progressive Caucus,

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:52.351
President Biden reportedly said
that he's frustrated

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:54.954
with Senators
Joe Manchin and Kyrsten Sinema.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:58.158
Well, you know it's bad when
a 78-year-old man is on Zoom

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.993
and that's not
the frustrating part.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:02.562
[ Laughter ]
During a briefing yesterday,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.598
White House Press Secretary
Jen Psaki showed a chart

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.535
of how much debt was accumulated
under former President Trump

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.769
and said, "Republicans spent

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:13.506
like drunken sailors
over the last four years."

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.309
And, in some cases,
they also looked like them.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.743
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.513
Former White House Press
Secretary Stephanie Grisham's

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.847
book was released today.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:22.849
Find it in the

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.951
Complicit But Needs Money
section.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.921
[ Laughter ]
The New York Times published
an op-ed yesterday titled

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.089
"What's Wrong
With Kyrsten Sinema?"

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:33.326
Well, for one thing,
I think she may be color blind?

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.827
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:37.630
Former presidential candidate
Andrew Yang announced yesterday

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.898
that he has changed
his voting registration

00:01:39.898 --> 00:01:42.901
from Democrat to Independent,
raising the question,

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:46.773
"If a tree falls in the woods,
can we listen to that,

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.409
instead of Andrew Yang?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.377
And, finally,
the rights to the Folgers

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.613
"The best part of waking up"
jingle

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.448
recently sold at auction
for more than $90,000,

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:58.584
while the Kars4Kids jingle

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.820
was taken out back
and shot in the head.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.155
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:04.224
That was a monologue.

